id: pm-9djr6d
title: Edit linked-test metadata in place with preserved provenance and atomic history
description: "Implement the complete GH1419 linked-test editor under the existing universal metadata reference lineage. Patch only explicit supported metadata fields; retain list position, immutable creation provenance and unchanged fields; stamp editor identity and time; reject empty or ambiguous selectors atomically; expose the same SDK operation through CLI and MCP."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T15:39:56.760Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T18:12:45.693Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-11T18:07:59.143Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-11T18:07:59.143Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: CLI and SDK edit one linked test by exact selector or one-based index; unchanged fields and original provenance survive; changed edit writes one field-level history event and editor metadata; equal retry preserves authoritative bytes; absent or ambiguous selectors refuse without mutation; invalid context patches are refused before persistence; command changes require fresh provenance/trust rather than preserving authorization; packed Node and Bun transports agree.
goal: project management = context management
parent: pm-gh1381
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "One locked metadata patch preserves list order, command and original provenance, stamps the editor, emits granular tests_update history and skips normalized no-op writes. Exact index/command/path selectors and malformed edits fail atomically."
expected_result: "Correct metadata without recreating a test or losing provenance, with consistent typed SDK and transport behavior."
actual_result: "Canonical sandboxed coverage passes 10,163 tests across 798 files with exact statements 68097/68097, branches 52238/52238, functions 14040/14040 and lines 64757/64757. Typecheck and all static subgates pass after planning-field and typed-edge repairs, including graph/record assurance and mutation controls. Linked editor and transport regressions, packed Node 24/26 and Bun consumers, strict declarations, npx/bunx smoke, history verification and four-direction published workspace compatibility pass; invalid and no-op edits retain authoritative bytes."
